**Read:** [Sistemas elétricos de potência — Arlei Bichels](../sources/Sistemas-Eletricos-de-Potencia-Bichels.lingua#r_5T4SVBJ6FAPQWJPVNQV4Y6427G), entire text and complete applicable examples; [MATPOWER User’s Manual, version 8.1](../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV), all model, power-flow and continuation chapters; [PowerModels.jl — formulations, methods and primary paper](../sources/PowerModels-Methods-and-Formulations.lingua#r_3SDQSM0EXY38699XFME0NQQT2H), complete relevant formulation/result definitions; [Power Grid Library — OPF benchmarks and provenance](../sources/Power-Grid-Library-OPF-Benchmarks.lingua#r_6AC54N8ECBG43CFWW99NERNWN5), whole selected model/report and actual case provenance.

Read all of [Sistemas elétricos de potência — Arlei Bichels](../sources/Sistemas-Eletricos-de-Potencia-Bichels.lingua#r_5T4SVBJ6FAPQWJPVNQV4Y6427G) and the entire [MATPOWER User’s Manual, version 8.1](../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV) model/flow/continuation treatment, then work a versioned authorized benchmark or an original clearly specified network. Reconstruct branch, generator, load, tap and shunt equations with consistent bases and source conventions.

Compare polar and rectangular or current-balance formulations, independent derivatives and several initial conditions. Check bus/branch balances, losses and every declared device/network limit. Use the original two-bus polynomial as an exact restricted benchmark before the larger network. Demonstrate a controlled case with multiple/no steady solutions or a binding reactive/control limit.

Trace loading through continuation, diagnose conditioning and compare the result with a direct solve and an independently predicted changed state. Separate a mathematical branch/fold from dynamic voltage recovery and usable operating capacity. Carry input/model uncertainty and topology changes into the conclusion. Produce complete derivations, original calculation inputs, residual/convergence evidence and a defended physical interpretation that another reader can reconstruct; a solver screenshot or successful exit status is insufficient.

